      "Shadow",
      "visual",
      "box-shadow",
      1,
      "shadow.presets",
      "role corrected 'color' -> 'visual' 2026-08-07. A box-shadow VALUE is not a colour (offset/blur/spread precede it), and the sibling 'BoxShadow' row below already said 'visual' — the table disagreed with itself about one property. That disagreement was load-bearing in two ways: (1) 18 live attrs (cardShadow/shadowHover/gridItemShadow/tileShadow/badgeImageShadow/...) carried role='color', so db_lookup.attr_is_colour_role admitted them and the converter's colour gate treated a shadow as a colour; (2) property_suffixes is read 'ORDER BY rowid LIMIT 1', and 'Shadow' precedes 'BoxShadow', so for css_property='box-shadow' the WRONG row won by file order alone. Both rows now agree, so the row-order tie-break for this property is no longer decidable-by-accident. Measured before/after: role='color' rows whose css_property contains no colour at all, 19 -> 1.",
      null
